### Why this is a stop and not a start

The card's step 1 modifies `chase_candidates.py` (adding `--member/--owner/--offset/--type` for one
arbitrary member while leaving the all-open-rows default output untouched) and step 2 wraps it with
`chase_judge.py`. Both must be read for their contracts, but the deferred prerequisite is precisely
the record that says which of the two stages is finished, which member/owner/offset/type conventions
it settled on, and what the existing default output is. Building the single-member mode on top of an
unpublished pipeline would either duplicate its interface or contradict it — the same failure mode the
backlog rules call out for `out`-row re-litigation. No value here is worth guessing at.

### What unblocks it (one step)

Publish `tmp/freebuff/reports/chase-candidates.md` with `STATUS: done` for the chase-candidates card
(its `Tools/scripts/chase/chase_candidates.py` is already on disk, 443 lines), then re-run this card.
